%N A398521 Decimal expansion of Sum_{k>=1} tau(k)/(k*(k+1)), where tau(k) = A000005(k) is the number of divisors of k.
%C A398521 This constant appears in the asymptotic formula for A398520.
%H A398521 Olivier Bordellès, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1142/S1793042122501056">On certain sums of number theory</a>, International Journal of Number Theory, Vol. 18, No. 9  (2022), pp. 2053-2074; <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2009.05751v2">arXiv preprint</a>, arXiv:2009.05751 [math.NT], 2020.
%H A398521 Ling Li, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.20400">On the Hyperbolic Fractional Sum of the Divisor Function</a>, arXiv:2604.20400 [math.NT], 2026.
%H A398521 Kui Liu, Jie Wu, and Zhishan Yang, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1142/S179304212450043X">On some sums involving the integral part function</a>, International Journal of Number Theory, Vol. 20, No. 3 (2024), pp. 831-847; <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2109.01382">arXiv preprint</a>, arXiv:2109.01382 [math.NT], 2021.
%H A398521 Jing Ma and Huayan Sun, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1007/s10998-020-00378-3">On a sum involving the divisor function</a>, Periodica Mathematica Hungarica, Vol. 83, No. 2 (2021), pp. 185-191.
%H A398521 Joshua Stucky, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jnt.2021.09.015">The fractional sum of small arithmetic functions</a>, Journal of Number Theory, Vol. 238 (2022), pp. 731-739; <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2106.14142">arXiv preprint</a>, arXiv:2106.14142 [math.NT], 2021.
%H A398521 Wei Zhang, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jnt.2023.10.011">On a variant of the prime number theorem</a>, Journal of Number Theory, Vol. 257 (2024), pp. 163-185; <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2303.12347">arXiv preprint</a>, arXiv:2303.12347 [math.NT], 2023.
%F A398521 Equals 1/2 + Sum_{k>=2} (-1)^k * (D(k) - 1), where D(s) = zeta(s)^2 is the Dirichlet g.f. of tau.
%e A398521 1.880770870193601660684417478612569884269820208997451...
%o A398521 (PARI) suminf(k = 2, (-1)^k * (zeta(k)^2 - 1)) + 1/2
